<title>GERMANY: German air cargo market up 6.9pct in December 1996.</title>
<headline>German air cargo market up 6.9pct in December 1996.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air cargo flown to and from Germany rose 6.9 percent in December 1996 to 175,998 tonnes, the monthly traffic report of the German airports association ADV said.</p>
<p>The following table shows total, flown and trucked air cargo volumes in tonnes at international German airports in December 1996.</p>
<p> Airport	   Flown     Trucked   Total   Pct change</p>
<p> Berlin(total)     4,058     598     4,646   up  49.3</p>
<p> -Tegel		1,486     573     2,059   up   6.9</p>
<p> -Tempelhof	     21	 0	  21   up  23.5</p>
<p> -Schoenefeld	2,551	25     2,576   up 119.4</p>
<p> Bremen		  243   2,000     2,243   up  27.5</p>
<p> Dresden		 140     219	 359   up   9.1</p>
<p> Duesseldorf	 5,694   4,030     9,724   up   1.1</p>
<p> Frankfurt	 120,413     n/a	 n/a</p>
<p> Hamburg	     3,052   2,479     5,531   up   4.7</p>
<p> Hanover	     1,208     n/a	 n/a</p>
<p> Cologne	    27,093   3,246    30,339   up   7.7</p>
<p> Leipzig/Halle	 237     121	 358   up   5.3</p>
<p> Munich		8,508     n/a	 n/a</p>
<p> Muenster		 53   1,016     1,069   up   7.7</p>
<p> Nuremberg	   3,848   2,358     6,206   up   2.1</p>
<p> Saarbruecken	   11     185	 196   up  21.7</p>
<p> Stuttgart	   1,690   4,427     6,117   up   3.9</p>
<p> TOTAL	     175,998     n/a	 n/a</p>
<p>*Notes: No overall air cargo total is given as several large airports with known large trucking volumes do not release trucking figures.</p>
<p>Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
